---
description: Never add AI attribution to git commits or pull requests
alwaysApply: true
---

When creating or amending a git commit, or creating/updating a pull request, never add
AI attribution: no `Co-authored-by` trailer naming Claude, Cursor, Copilot or Codex, no
"Generated with Claude Code" or "Made with Cursor" footer, and no `Made-with:`,
`Claude-Session:` or `Agent-Logs-Url:` trailer. Keep `Co-authored-by` lines for real
human collaborators.

After every commit, run
`git log -1 --format=%B | grep -n -i -E '^(co-authored-by|generated[- ]with|claude-session|made-with|agent-logs-url)'`
and, if it finds an AI-attribution line, amend the commit to remove it before finishing.
